  "result": "Perfect! All 101 tests pass. Here's a summary of what I've added for VAT (Value Added Tax):\n\n**Added to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`lineVAT(line)`** \u2014 Calculates VAT for a single line:\n   - VAT is computed on the line amount AFTER discount\n   - Formula: (qty \u00d7 unitPrice - discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n   - Result is rounded per line using `roundCents()`\n   - Example: \u20ac100 line with 10% discount and 21% VAT \u2192 (\u20ac90 \u00d7 21%) = \u20ac18.90\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n   - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals (before discount)\n   - `discount` = sum of line discounts\n   - `vat` = sum of rounded line VATs (not a percentage of total)\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat\n\n**Updated `src/render.js`:**\n- Added VAT line in plain-text invoice output, displayed just above the total\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acxx.xx`\n\n**Key VAT behavior:**\n- VAT is calculated PER LINE on the discounted amount, then rounded\n- VAT rates in catalogue: 21% (most items), 9% (printed materials), 0% (exempt items)\n- Invoice VAT = sum of per-line VATs, NOT calculated as a percentage of invoice total\n- All amounts (line totals, discounts, VAT, totals) clamped at 0 (no negatives)\n\n**Tests added (12 new tests):**\n- `lineVAT` calculation with/without discounts, different VAT rates\n- `invoiceTotals` returns correct structure with VAT\n- VAT calculations with discounts and mixed rates\n- `renderInvoiceText` displays VAT line correctly\n\nExample invoice calculation:\n- 5 \u00d7 \u20ac95.00 dev hours, 0% discount, 21% VAT\n- Subtotal: \u20ac475.00\n- Discount: \u20ac0.00\n- VAT: \u20ac99.75\n- Total: \u20ac574.75",
